[38;5;231m⏺[39m Done. [38;5;153mindex.html[39m now has a single native checkbox in [38;5;153m<main>[39m, wrapped in a [38;5;153m<label>[39m so clicking the text toggles it,
  with one CSS rule that strikes through the label when checked.

  - No JavaScript, no dependencies — checked/unchecked state and keyboard toggling come from the browser.
  - The [38;5;153m<span>[39m exists only to give the CSS sibling selector something to target.

  I did not run any tests: the repo has no test setup, and standing one up for a static checkbox would be well beyond
  the change. I also didn't open it in a browser — the markup is a standard native checkbox, but if you want it verified
  visually, say so and I'll load it.

